  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\alpha=\\frac{1}{\\sin 60^{\\circ} \\sin 61^{\\circ}}+\\frac{1}{\\sin 62^{\\circ} \\sin 63^{\\circ}}+\\ldots+\\frac{1}{\\sin 118^{\\circ} \\sin 119^{\\circ}}$\nThen the value of $\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec} 1^{\\circ}}{\\alpha}\\right)^2$ is __________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\alpha=\\sum_{\\mathrm{r}-30}^{59} \\frac{1}{\\sin (2 \\mathrm{r})^{\\circ} \\sin (2 \\mathrm{r}+1)^{\\circ}} \\\\ & \\frac{\\alpha}{\\operatorname{cosec} 1^{\\circ}}=\\sum_{\\mathrm{r}-30}^{59} \\frac{\\sin 1^{\\circ}}{\\sin (2 \\mathrm{r})^{\\circ} \\sin (2 \\mathrm{r}+1)^{\\circ}} \\\\ & =\\sum_{\\mathrm{r}-30}^{59}\\left(\\cot (2 \\mathrm{r})^{\\circ}-\\cot (2 \\mathrm{r}+1)^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\ & =\\cot 60^{\\circ}-\\cot 61^{\\circ} \\\\ & \\quad+\\cot 62^{\\circ}-\\cot 63^{\\circ} \\\\ & \\quad \\vdots \\\\ & +\\cot \\left(118^{\\circ}\\right)-\\cot \\left(119^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\ & \\frac{\\alpha}{\\operatorname{cosec} 1^{\\circ}}=\\cot 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ & \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec} 1^{\\circ}}{\\alpha}\\right)^2=3\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
